Portions of `Sources/Stripe/Models`, `Sources/Stripe/Requests` and
`Sources/Stripe/Shared` are derived from swift-stripe-standard
(https://github.com/swift-standards/swift-stripe-standard), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Those sources in turn carry file headers attributing earlier work by
Andrew Edwards and Anthony Castelli, originating in stripe-kit
(https://github.com/vapor-community/stripe-kit), licensed under the MIT License.

The model types were vendored and then modified:

  * the 86-module structure was flattened into a single `Stripe` target;
  * routing, client-witness, and dependency-injection machinery was removed;
  * resource identifiers are plain `String` typealiases, replacing the
    `Tagged` phantom-type wrapper and swift-tagged-primitives;
  * redundant snake_case `CodingKeys` raw values were removed in favour of
    `JSONDecoder.KeyDecodingStrategy.convertFromSnakeCase`, which fixes fields
    that previously decoded to `nil`;
  * three upstream field-name defects were corrected (see README).
